# Gatekeeper, fingerprints and a Keystore shared-secret participant in one
# service, so both kinds of auth token carry the key Keystore negotiated. The
# fingerprint reader is the host user's, through the device broker's socket
# the supervisor binds into the cell; fprintd's results come from the
# supervisor. It runs as root: Android's system user is the host user, so its
# keys and records stay in a folder only root reads. Android's fingerprint
# service reads the enrollment generation beside it.
on post-fs-data
    mkdir /data/vendor/droidloom-authentication 0750 root system
    mkdir /data/vendor/droidloom-authentication/private 0700 root root

service vendor.authentication-droidloom /vendor/bin/hw/droidloom-authentication-service
    class hal
    user root
    group root
    interface aidl android.hardware.gatekeeper.IGatekeeper/default
    interface aidl android.hardware.biometrics.fingerprint.IFingerprint/default
    interface aidl android.hardware.security.sharedsecret.ISharedSecret/droidloom
    stdio_to_kmsg
